# Everflowing Chalice's "This artifact enters with a charge counter on it for each time it was kicked" is a replacement
# effect of its own (CR 614.1c). CR 614.12: which replacement effects apply is judged on the permanent as it would exist on the
# battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent". Under March
# of the Machines ("Each noncreature artifact is an artifact creature with power and toughness each equal to its mana value",
# layers 4 and 7b) the Chalice would be an artifact creature there, so Humility ("All creatures lose all abilities and have
# base power and toughness 1/1", layers 6 and 7b), later than March, takes its abilities: kicked once, it enters with no
# charge counter, a 1/1 (Humility's base power and toughness applies after March's, by timestamp). The positive control of
# the counter is everflowing-chalice-kicked-once-enters-with-one-charge-counter-and-taps-for-one-colorless. Black Lotus pays
# for March, so no other artifact is left for March to make a 0/0; Ancient Tomb deals Bot1 2 damage.

